{#
	Next case study, at the foot of a work single.

	Derived navigation, not content. Like breadcrumbs and pagination it comes
	from the query rather than from ACF — an authored "next project" field
	would drift the moment a project is inserted between two others, and the
	drift would be silent.

	The title is wrapped in <bdi>: a project name is usually Latin inside a
	Hebrew page, and without isolation the surrounding direction reorders it.

	Figma: `next-project` on Inner Pages / Desktop (57:281) and Mobile (85:139).
#}

{% if project %}
	<nav class="next-project" aria-label="ניווט בין פרויקטים">
		<div class="container">
			<a class="next-project__link" href="{{ project.link }}">
				<span class="next-project__meta">
					<span class="next-project__label">הפרויקט הבא</span>
					<span class="next-project__title"><bdi>{{ project.title }}</bdi></span>
				</span>

				{# Decorative: the link text already says where this goes. #}
				<span class="next-project__arrow" aria-hidden="true">←</span>
			</a>
		</div>
	</nav>
{% endif %}
